{"game": "risk-of-rain-returns", "language": "english", "appid": 1337520, "month": "2026-07", "window": 3, "start_date": 1784160000, "end_date": 1784851199, "month_true_total": 54, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 00:55:52 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "231159138", "author": {"steamid": "76561198682439406", "personaname": "SaggyPaulZ", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198682439406/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 2863, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 73, "playtime_at_review": 2357, "last_played": 1791313112, "avatar": "e2c5bfc62b56a9aac49b79bb55a0bd24a0db7e71"}, "language": "english", "review": "I had originally played Risk of Rain on Xbox, and upon buying my computer the first game I knew I had to get was RoR Returns. The Risk of Rain franchise is my personal favorite rouge like, because it provides a ,unique gameplay loop, powerful stacking items, interesting and difficult challenges, and finally captivating story and mystery. RoR Returns is a high quality and expansive remaster, providing new characters, features, and challenges that put the difficulty of the original game to shame. I have yet to master the game, or come anywhere near 100%, but I know the grind will be fun the whole ride through. I cannot recommend this game or the Risk of Rain franchise enough, they are the greatest games of their kind. (even better than The Binding of Issac, imo)", "timestamp_created": 1784848769, "timestamp_updated": 1784848769, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1699469751", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "231156938", "author": {"steamid": "76561198754974727", "personaname": "Sivilisk", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://stea